abstract: >
  Hydra is an open-source multi-physics computational framework that composes
  specialized CFD solvers into coupled simulation pipelines. It orchestrates
  modular solver libraries — covering compressible Euler and Navier–Stokes flows, 
  real fluid dynamics, chemical kinetics, solid heat conduction, radiative heat transfer, 
  and particle tracking — through a unified build system and command-line interface. 
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - multi-physics
  - conjugate heat transfer
  - compressible flow
  - particle tracking
  - reactive flows
  - radiative heat transfer
  - Fortran
  - OpenMP
  - MPI
